#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157102 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2981f6-bfbf-5c1e-a4a2-2814dc24804a" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Quadratic Function Where X Is a Function of Y"}] :question/id #uuid "e6282f0a-7891-5261-968e-63aa42421d00" :question/math-academy-id "e-7822" :question/problem "Plot the graph of $x=-2y^2 - 3y$." :question/worked-solution "To plot $x=-2y^2-3y$, we will first plot the function $y=-2x^2-3x$ and then reflect it over the line $y=x$.\n\nThe curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ is a parabola. It has the following factored form:\n\n$$\ny = -x(2x+3)\n$$\n\nFrom the factored form above, we see that we have a negative parabola with roots at $x=0$ and\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac32\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2978/Source/Images/eeaacf8a6bbb54443c4408fc71d42f79.png)\n\nNow, to get the curve $x=-2y^2-3y$, we just have to reflect the curve $y=-2x^2-3x$ over the line $y=x$, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2978/Source/Images/7f7897c5d0cd6a834e27c7a6307c2154.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1f2981f6-bfbf-5c1e-a4a2-2814dc24804a" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Quadratic Function Where X Is a Function of Y"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "968abc8c-0588-5fc9-b2b4-060842365e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2978/Source/Images/q-88341-a-1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156629} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bbcc7e-259f-54d4-aaaa-0ab3044248b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2978/Source/Images/q-88341-a-2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156630} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c730aa-7833-5807-aebd-06881aba37ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2978/Source/Images/q-88341-a-5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 